 "final_message": "All twelve items are done, and the test suite passes (6 tests, including the two new ones). I haven't added tests for the other fixes, so those were only checked by the existing tests.\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** each function in `metrics.py`, `loader.py` and `report.py` now follows its SPEC section. A few details you might not assume:\n  - `parse_transcript_log` raises `ValueError` with `line N` for any `flagged` value other than `1`, `0` or empty. SPEC lists only those three but doesn't say what to do with anything else, so that was my call.\n  - `flags_in_window` returns `0` for negative `days` as well as for `0`.\n  - `top_flagged_groups` returns an empty list for a negative `n`.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added a test that a `None` value counts as not flagged, and one that `dedupe_transcripts` keeps the last transcript for a duplicate id.\n- **Item 11:** the README `flags_in_window` entry now says it sums the last `days` entries. I added a `daily_flag_counts` entry.\n- **Item 12:** I checked the rest against SPEC and fixed these:\n  - `flag_rate_by_group` now maps empty groups to `None` and orders keys by group name.\n  - `top_flagged_groups` excludes empty groups and breaks ties by group name.\n  - `longest_positive_streak` now resets the run on a zero entry. Before, it counted non-adjacent positives as one run.\n  - I also reworded the README's `dedupe_transcripts` entry to say it keeps the last transcript per id.",
